    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of the change I implemented.\n\n## What the change does\nWhen creating an owner via `POST /api/owners`, `registrationDate` is now optional. If the client omits it, the server sets it to the current date; if supplied, the given date is kept. The date is stored and returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format.\n\n## Files changed\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields`, this makes the field both accepted on input (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and returned on output (`OwnerDto`), generated as `java.time.LocalDate`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field mapped to a `registration_date` DATE column, with getter/setter and the `java.time.LocalDate` import.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`** \u2014 After MapStruct maps the request to an `Owner`, it defaults `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` when null. (MapStruct auto-maps the supplied value by matching name/type, so a supplied date flows through unchanged.)\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 Added the nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\n5. **DB seed data** (`db/{hsqldb,mysql}/data.sql`) \u2014 The positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)` seed rows needed the extra trailing `NULL` for the new column (h2/postgres already used explicit column lists, so they were untouched).\n\n## Verification\nBoth new acceptance tests pass \u2014 `coreDefaultsToToday` (omitted date \u2192 today) and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate` (supplied `2020-06-15` preserved) \u2014 and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with 0 failures/errors.",
